n we're going to be  calling our figure function and we're  going to be giving y range to our car  list  the y range is basically just going to  have the different values which are  going to be present on the y axis we've  given the blot a width of 800 and a  height of 600  the title of the plot is cars with top  horsepower and the x-axis label is  horsepower  the tools that we're using here is pan  box select zoom in zoom out save and  reset so these are tools that you're  going to be getting on the right side of  your plot  now let's render our glyph or render our  graph  the graph that we are going to be using  here is the horizontal bar graph so the  y axis is going to have cars  and the right or basically the height of  the entire bar is going to depend on the  horsepower  the left is going to start from 0 and  the height of each bar is going to be  0.4  the color that we are going to be giving  is going to be a palette of blue so each  different car will have a different  color of blue associated with it and  the  color of blue which is associated with  it will depend on the car list  now fill alpha 0.9 the source is your  source data that you have over here  which is the column data source of our  data frame  and the legend is going to be car which  basically means that your entire uh  plot is going to have the legend of car  now we're gonna be adding the legend  this is  us giving the legend its orientation so  the legend is going to be vertically  oriented the location is going to be on  the top right and the font size of the  text car of a legend is going to be 10  px or 10 pixels  we're also going to be adding a hover  tool  inside this harvard tool this hover tool  tips will basically tell you what you're  going to be seeing  in the harvard toolbox  so we're going to be creating this with  the help of an html format  the first thing that you're going to be  seeing is the name of the car  the next  column will have the price of the car  the horsepower of 